  "integration": {
    "summary": "Set coil 17 = 1 (communicating mode; the map says it mirrors parameter P22), then drive the unit with the Y1/Y2/G/W2/humidity/O call coils (0-4, 24). Read temperatures, relay states, pressure switches and the alarm word (input register 18) to monitor it.",
    "minimum_registers": [
      {
        "table": "coil",
        "address": 17,
        "why": "Communicating (Modbus) thermostat mode"
      },
      {
        "table": "coil",
        "address": 0,
        "why": "Y1 cooling call"
      },
      {
        "table": "coil",
        "address": 3,
        "why": "G fan call"
      },
      {
        "table": "discrete_input",
        "address": 13,
        "why": "Compressor 1 relay state"
      },
      {
        "table": "input_register",
        "address": 18,
        "why": "Alarm status bits"
      },
      {
        "table": "input_register",
        "address": 14,
        "why": "P1 temperature"
      },
      {
        "table": "input_register",
        "address": 27,
        "why": "Outdoor temperature"
      },
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 8,
        "why": "Modbus timeout (minutes)"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "In the source manual's configuration menu set item 23 (T'STAT Select; item numbers may differ in the other manuals that share this table) to C for a communicating thermostat via Modbus, or write coil 17 = 1 (the Modbus map says coil 17 reads and changes 'P22', the thermostat-type setting). The Modbus ID (item 24, 1-99, default 1) and baud (item 25: 9.6 or 19 = 9600/19200) are set in the board configuration menu.",
    "watchdog": "Register 8 / configuration item 26 sets the Modbus timeout (1-60 min, default 10). After that long without Modbus traffic the board falls back to hardware thermostat calls.",
    "quirks": [
      "Only single-coil (05) and single-register (06) writes are accepted.",
      "Register reads are documented with function 04 only, including the writable ones.",
      "Temperature value 255 means no sensor or a failed sensor."
    ],
    "setup": [
      "Default slave ID 1, 19200 baud, 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit.",
      "The board has two RJ11 Modbus ports wired in parallel; both carry the same bus."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Until the thermostat type is C (menu item 23, or coil 17 = 1) the board keeps following its hardwired thermostat inputs.",
      "After the Modbus timeout with no traffic the board switches back to its hardware thermostat inputs, so poll faster than the timeout."
    ]
  },
  "verified": {
    "date": "2026-11-19",
    "method": "independent re-check of every register against the source PDF"
  }
